  "pr_title": "feat(plugin): download and run the standalone CLI",
  "pr_description": "## Goal\n\nTeammates install only the Obsidian plugin. The plugin downloads and runs the standalone CLI of its own version, so teammates need no Terminal, Python, uv, Node, or pnpm.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe new module `obsidian-plugin/standalone-cli.ts` installs the standalone CLI. The plugin uses this module when the `cliPath` setting is empty. An empty path is now the default. The module downloads `spsync-macos-arm64.tar.gz` and `spsync-macos-arm64.tar.gz.sha256` from the GitHub release `v<plugin version>`. It checks the SHA-256 checksum before it unpacks the archive. When the checksum does not match, the plugin shows an error and does not install or run the build.\n\nAll vaults share one install root, `~/Library/Application Support/spsync/bin/`. The module unpacks each download with `/usr/bin/tar` into a separate staging folder. Then it renames the folder to `<version>/` in one atomic step. Thus a version folder exists only after its checksum check passed, and two vaults that install at the same time cannot run a partial build. After a successful install, the module removes older versions and stale staging folders. It keeps newer versions, because a vault with a newer plugin version can still use them.\n\nThe plugin starts the install when the workspace layout is ready, so the first command does not wait for the download. A sticky notice shows the download progress. Commands that start during the install wait for the same install. A failed download shows an error that names the URL. On an Intel Mac, the plugin shows an error that points to the `cliPath` setting, because the release publishes only an Apple silicon build. A non-empty `cliPath` setting skips the download. The plugin does not migrate a saved `~/.local/bin/spsync` value to empty, because a developer can set that path on purpose.\n\nThe plugin now has unit tests that run with Node's built-in test runner (`pnpm -C obsidian-plugin run test`). The pre-commit hook runs these tests. The README describes the BRAT install for teammates and the `cliPath` override for developers. The change does not touch docx reading or patching.\n\n## Testing\n\n- New `node:test` tests in `obsidian-plugin/standalone-cli.test.ts` use a real tar archive and a fake release server. They cover the first install and later runs without a download, two parallel installs, a checksum mismatch, a failed download, the removal of older versions, and the Intel Mac error.\n- `standaloneCli` ran against the real `v0.1.0` release with Node `fetch`. It installed the build, and `spsync --version` printed `spsync 0.1.0` with `PATH=/usr/bin:/bin`.\n- `pnpm -C obsidian-plugin run format:check`, `lint`, `test`, and `build` pass.\n- `uv run ruff format --check`, `uv run ruff check`, `uv run ty check`, `uv run anti-slop-python src tests`, and `uv run pytest` pass.\n- Manual check needed in Obsidian after the next release: install the plugin with BRAT from `jekozyra/spsync` on a Mac without Python, uv, or Node. Confirm the download notice, and confirm that \"Sync this note\" works. Then open a second vault, and confirm that it uses the same build without a second download.\n\n## Issue\n\nCloses #8\n"
